even if you're the most hardened of PTSD  ridden Dark Souls veterans there are  some things you should know before  diving headfirst into the frustration  and blood filled swimming pool that is  blood-borne there are three starting  weapons to choose from in blood-borne  each with its own strengths weaknesses  and quirks the saw cleaver is the most  balanced starting weapon hence why it's  appeared in most early blood-borne  footage it balances the quickness of a  lighter blade with the heft and power of  a heavier weapon making it the ideal  starter especially for those unfamiliar  with the soul genre the other two  weapons are more polarizing the threaded  cane is quick and nimble but it does  significantly less damage while the  hunter's axe is big and slow but it  dulls out the hurt most efficiently all  three weapons have the ability to extend  with l1 increasing their reach but  diminishing their speed slightly the  threaded cane extends into a chain whip  the saw cleaver unfolds and the axe  extends into a two-handed pole axe while  the saw cleaver seems to have the  shortest range while extended it's more  powerful than the threaded cane and the  extended axe prevents you from holding a  gun in your offhand this will keep you  from parrying and using ranged attacks  which can be a severe disadvantage in  certain fights pick the weapon that  caters best to your play style whether  you like it slow and lumbering or fast  and furious and speaking of fast and  furious fans coming from the souls games  are going to notice blood-borne is  dominant focus on aggressive and mobile  tactics over playing it safe you're not  going to be relying on a heavy shield or  casting fireballs here so get used to  dodging and rolling around like a Cirque  de Soleil Acrobat with a gun well locked  onto enemies hitting circle is going to  allow you to dodge in sidestep giving  you opportunities to navigate around  your opponent for a backstab or get out  of the way when they're trying to devour  you when you're not locked on dodging  will cause you to dive roll a fair bit  further allowing you to get the hell  away from a dangerous situation or move  behind a foe in one fell swoop it's also  worth noting that hitting your heavy  attack r2 at the same time you press  forward will trigger a heavy jump strike  allowing you to close the distance in  the same way a roll would but with all  the striking force of your strong attack  because you'll be pretty much shield  listen blood-borne armor is going to  take on additional importance in keeping  you alive before you engage the cleric  beast blood burns first boss you'll want  to either purchase the first set of  armor from the hunters dream when you've  saved up around 3,000 blood echoes or if  you're feeling thrifty and you've spent  all your money on vials the same set of  armor is available to be found deep  within the sewers don't be  - intimidated it may not be on route to  the cleric beast but the sewers are of a  fairly manageable difficulty and you'll  be handsomely rewarded for your bravery  with a hot news at armor don't be afraid  to drop your blood echoes on that same  set of armor though you most likely  won't beat the first boss in your first  attempt so you might as well invest  before you lose everything  say it with me now there are no souls in  blood-borne there are only blood echoes  hell I still call them Souls but here's  what you need to know about them whether  they're echoes or not  they virtually serve the exact same  purpose that souls did in the previous  Souls game allowing you to purchase  items and gear repair and fortify  weapons level up your skills and a  number of other things throughout the  game as you may have expected you'll  drop all your blood echoes upon death  but you'll have the chance to retrieve  them from the scene of your previous  death as long as you don't die on your  way there one change in blood-borne is  that enemies can pick up your  blood-stained forcing you to kill a  specific enemy to retrieve your  hard-earned echoes you can identify the  target enemy by their ethereal glowing  eyes which will help locate them but it  definitely won't help you kill them at  first you'll be wondering where to level  up as you explore the game's hub world  see that creepy sleeping doll in the  corner fight the Clara feast and either  win or die in the doll will awaken  allowing you to pour all your blood  echoes into levelling up I recommend you  do so lest you lose thirty thousand  echoes dying in a cave somewhere but  you'll need at least one insight in the  bank to cash in  finally a more general tip don't fear  grinding in blood-borne blood vials will  serve as your Estus flask replacement  here allowing you to regain health  fairly quickly and they're dropped  really frequently by even the easiest  enemies a failed boss fight is going to  drain your blood vials and quick silver  bullets in short order so don't be too  proud to get back on your feet by taking  on some manageable enemies to grind out  vials gear levels before walking back  into that nightmare fog for another bout  there's a lot more to say about  blood-borne but we really don't want to  spoil anything more of this excellent  game for you at least not in this video  so good luck out there oh and before you  go let me just introduce you to your new  best friend that you died screen you'll  be seeing a lot of him
 

